2026-10-08 12:14:53        "extracted_fact": "A useful year-over-year signal appears in the learner segment. Azure DevOps usage among respondents learning to code moved from\nThat does not prove a broad product slowdown, but it does show Azure DevOps remains far more established in professional environments than in early learning communities.\n2. Azure DevOps Usage & Adoption Statistics\nAzure DevOps is positioned as an end-to-end delivery platform rather than a single-purpose tool. Microsoft describes it as a way to “share code, track work, and ship software,” and the product stack spans Azure Boards, Azure Pipelines, Azure Repos, Azure Test Plans, and Azure Artifacts.\nIn practical terms, that means Azure DevOps remains strongest where organizations want one place for planning, source control, CI/CD, testing, and package management.\nRea",
2026-10-08 12:14:53        "excerpt": "A useful year-over-year signal appears in the learner segment. Azure DevOps usage among respondents learning to code moved from\nThat does not prove a broad product slowdown, but it does show Azure DevOps remains far more established in professional environments than in early learning communities.\n2. Azure DevOps Usage & Adoption Statistics\nAzure DevOps is positioned as an end-to-end delivery platform rather than a single-purpose tool. Microsoft describes it as a way to “share code, track work, and ship software,” and the product stack spans Azure Boards, Azure Pipelines, Azure Repos, Azure Test Plans, and Azure Artifacts.\nIn practical terms, that means Azure DevOps remains strongest where organizations want one place for planning, source control, CI/CD, testing, and package management.\nRead our blog on the best Azure Devops code review tools →",
