2026-10-09 01:15:54        "extracted_fact": "Explore the market potential with our data-driven report\nAutomotive and Transportation Functional Safety Market Outlook\nThe global automotive and transportation functional safety market size was USD 1.9 billion in 2024, and it will grow by 9.5% during 2025–2032, to reach USD 3.9 billion by 2032.\nThe market growth is driven by the increasing development in the vehicle electronics and software systems, mainly focusing on ADAS, EVs, and self-driving technologies. As vehicles increasingly become a technologically dense, with safety operations controlled by intricate software, strong functional safety becomes essential to prevent system malfunction and ensure passenger safety. As per the World Health Organization (WHO), over 1.35 million people worldwide die in traffic accidents yearly, which h",
2026-10-09 01:15:54        "excerpt": "Explore the market potential with our data-driven report\nAutomotive and Transportation Functional Safety Market Outlook\nThe global automotive and transportation functional safety market size was USD 1.9 billion in 2024, and it will grow by 9.5% during 2025–2032, to reach USD 3.9 billion by 2032.\nThe market growth is driven by the increasing development in the vehicle electronics and software systems, mainly focusing on ADAS, EVs, and self-driving technologies. As vehicles increasingly become a technologically dense, with safety operations controlled by intricate software, strong functional safety becomes essential to prevent system malfunction and ensure passenger safety. As per the World Health Organization (WHO), over 1.35 million people worldwide die in traffic accidents yearly, which highlights the need for advanced vehicle safety systems.\nFunctional safety guarantees system operations are safe and reliable, even under critical conditions. Furthermore, automotive engineers and operations are currently focused on advanced automation, fault tolerance, and prevention of hazardous events even when one component fails. To achieve this, safety standards, such as ISO 26262, are applied. This is derived from the more-general IEC61508 safety standard of processes meant to provide safety lifecycle that can be integrated with electronic systems suitable for use.\nAutomotive and Transportation Functional Safety Market Emerging Trends",
